                <pb facs="0262" n="206" sameAs="frus:frus1876/pg206"/>

                <head>No. 105.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">General Schenck to Mr. Fish</hi>.</head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >London</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1876-03-02"><hi rendition="#italic">March</hi> 2,
                        1876</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>Lord Derby calls attention to third clause, subsection two, of extradition act,
                    and declines to give up Winslow unless promise is made by law or by arrangement
                    that he shall be tried only for the extradition crime.</p>
                <closer><signed>SCHENCK.</signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
